[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:Breakfast or Lunch?]
[00:13.38]Why was the writer's aunt surprised?
[00:19.69]It was Sunday.
[00:21.83]I never get up early on Sundays.
[00:25.34]I sometimes stay in bed until lunchtime.
[00:29.80]Last Sunday I got up very late.
[00:34.93]I looked out of the window.
[00:38.63]It was dark outside.
[00:42.30]'What a day!' I thought.
[00:45.79]'It's raining again.'
[00:48.79]Just then, the telephone rang.
[00:52.60]It was my aunt Lucy.
[00:55.64]'I've just arrived by train,' she said.
[00:59.67]'I'm coming to see you.'
[01:02.97]'But I'm still having breakfast,' I said.
[01:07.72]'What are you doing?' she asked.
[01:12.09]'I'm having breakfast,' I repeated.
[01:16.73]'Dear me,' she said.
[01:19.85]'Do you always get up so late? It's one o'clock!'
